cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  A Practical Hybrid VAE Framework for Parameter-Efficient
  Multiclass and Zero-Day Network Intrusion Detection
message: If you use this software or its findings, please cite the manuscript in paper/.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Vihaan
    family-names: Ovalekar
  - given-names: Ojas
    family-names: Gore
  - given-names: Yash
    family-names: Pradhan
  - given-names: Ishan
    family-names: Tanawade
abstract: >-
  Code and manuscript for a study of shortcut reliance in flow-based network intrusion
  detection. Introduces the Shortcut Reliance Ratio, an adversarial latent-level erasure
  method for the destination-port shortcut with removal verified by minimum description
  length, and a capacity sweep from 40,576 to 1,060 encoder parameters with deployment cost
  measured on a single CPU core.
keywords:
  - network intrusion detection
  - shortcut learning
  - variational autoencoder
  - concept erasure
  - edge computing
  - TinyML
license: MIT
